# A read from a receiver that is proven to be one of a few layouts is dispatched by a chain of shape tests, one case per layout.
# The failing side of the last test is unreachable, so the chain relies on the list of layouts being complete.
# Fault injection, testing=DropLastCase: the chain omits its last case, as if that layout were not in use. An object of that layout reaches the unreachable end.
# With --aot-harden=proof-checks (testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime) the receiver, as it entered the chain, is checked against the layouts of the cases before that end.
# If the check fails, the process crashes with a named error.
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime
# RIGHT: 18
# RIGHT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(WRONG): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=DropLastCase
# WRONG: crashed with SIGILL
# RUN(HELD): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=DropLastCase,CheckProofsAtRunTime
# HELD: bun: internal AOT error: type check failed
# HELD-NEXT: in the result of an operation
# HELD: crashed with SIGABRT
# -- source: main.ts
